column3:
"Through the appointment of an interim change director and a package of supporting consultancies contributing expertise and capacity, this project will mitigate the emergent risks (described elsewhere) to the success of Poole Museum’s capital project at a critical point in the investment cycle, ensuring it can meet its vision, mission and core objectives.

This project will ensure:
-	the museum is suitably resourced with freedom to use to best effect
-	a more secure and sustainable earned income and subsidy revenue base;
-	identify future capital and revenue external funding opportunities;
-	an adaptable ‘can do’ culture’;
-	the development of new services and partnerships as well as maintaining existing;
-	the museum meets and exceeds targets for audience development;
-	the Museum’s improved cultural standing and reputation in the conurbation and regionally;
-	meaningful engagement that makes a difference to the community and visitors that better meets people’s needs."
